From 25ff2bc0c4f9ea755bd7bcf0b90672d2e4fb68a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keith Packard <keithp@keithp.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 05:29:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/20] test-posix: Check sysconf's limits against <limits.h>
 and the system

<limits.h>'s minimum values and required constants, sysconf agreeing
with each runtime invariant value the header defines and never falling
below a runtime increasable one, the new names, the kernel's limits
seen in /proc/self/limits and /sys, and the limits where a test can
reach them: SYMLOOP_MAX links, MQ_OPEN_MAX descriptors, IOV_MAX
vectors, TZNAME_MAX names, SEM_VALUE_MAX and ATEXIT_MAX handlers.
ARG_MAX is checked by exec with arguments just under and just over it,
with several stack limits.
